# db-backend Project Overview

Java 17 / Spring Boot 4 / Spring Data JDBC / PostgreSQL layered monolith.

## Package map

| Package | Role |
|---------|------|
| `controller` | REST endpoints |
| `service` | Business orchestration |
| `repository` | Spring Data JDBC persistence |
| `dto/request`, `dto/response` | API contracts |
| `mapper` | Entity ↔ DTO mapping |
| `model` | Persistence entities (no API validation) |
| `exception` | `@RestControllerAdvice`, domain exceptions |
| `common` | Shared utilities (`ApiResponseBuilder`, `StringUtils`) |

## Request flow

`Controller` → `Service` → `Mapper` → `Repository` → PostgreSQL. Controllers never touch entities directly.

## Adding a new resource (copy User module)

1. Entity in `model/` (persistence only)
2. `{Entity}Repository` extending `CrudRepository`
3. DTOs in `dto/request` and `dto/response`
4. `{Entity}Mapper` in `mapper/`
5. `{Entity}Service` + `{Entity}Controller`
6. `api-testing/{resource}.http` — ad-hoc REST Client smoke requests (not part of the automated test suite)
7. `{Entity}ControllerTests` + `{Entity}ServiceTests`

## Conventions

- Constructor injection only; concrete `@Service` classes (no interfaces until needed)
- API paths: `/api/{resource-plural}`
- Secrets via env vars (`DB_DATASOURCE_*`); never commit `.env`
- Format with `./mvnw spotless:apply` before commit
- After code changes, follow `verification-workflow` — run `scripts/check.sh` before finishing

Reference implementation: `UserController`, `UserService`, `UserMapper`, `UpsertUserRequest`, `UserResponse`.
